            "severity": "HIGH",
            "location": "src/order.ts:100-108",
            "finding": "\"`markPaid`\" and \"`markFailed`\" do not check the current status, so a replayed or out-of-order webhook can flip a \"`paid`\" order to \"`failed`\" or mark a \"`cancelled`\" order (whose stock was already released) as \"`paid`\"; \"`markFailed`\" also never calls \"`releaseAll`\", so the stock reserved for failed payments stays reserved for good."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "SECURITY",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:12",
            "finding": "\"`SECRET`\" silently falls back to \"`\"\"`\" when \"`PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\" is unset, so anyone can compute valid signatures with an empty HMAC key; the module should fail fast when the secret is not configured."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "INTENT",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/api.ts:54-64",
            "finding": "The random \"`recommendations`\" shuffle for the start page, the customer order lookup \"`handleGetOrder`\", the unused \"`ordersOf`\" (src/store.ts:15), and the \"`notify.ts`\" to \"`mail.ts`\" HTML-mail rewrite are unrelated to payments and refunds and ride along as scope creep; the commit message mentions none of them."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "CLARITY",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "src/mail.ts:28-39",
            "finding": "The \"`catch`\" comment says \"the outbox job retries later\", but a mail that fails here never reaches the \"`outbox`\" and no retry job exists, so the comment is misleading."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "TESTING",
            "severity": "MEDIUM",
            "location": "src/webhook.ts:45-60",
            "finding": "None of the new security-sensitive logic (signature check, admin authorization, refund amounts, status transitions) has a test, and the project has no test script, so the defects above went unnoticed."
        },
        {
            "dimension": "DOCUMENTATION",
            "severity": "LOW",
            "location": "README.md:3-4",
            "finding": "The README feature list does not mention payment webhooks, admin refunds, order status, or confirmation mails, and does not document the required \"`PAYMENT_WEBHOOK_SECRET`\" environment variable."
        }
    ]
}
